strace
Usage: strace [-f] [-e trace=SET] CMD   |   strace -p PID

Traces the system calls a program makes -- every file it opens, socket it
connects, and why it exits. When a binary misbehaves and says nothing useful,
strace shows what it actually asked the kernel to do.

	-f                    follow child processes (forks)
	-e trace=open,openat  limit to these calls (also `network`, `file`)
	-p PID                attach to a process already running

See also: file, pspy, radare2
